{"nodes": [{"id": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_phase1_panel_compat_fail_closed_repair", "label": "Phase 1 Repair: Fail-Closed Panel-Compatibility Gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".local-evidence/golden-r11/R11-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT-PHASES-0-2.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Policy honoured: ungoverned classification must never create a safety exemption. The null-family branch is preserved verbatim because it serves loopParticipationCategories, an ADDITIVE loop obligation rather than an exemption, so nothing was over-blocked globally and non-Fire-Alarm packs are untouched. Live effect: 14 invalid Ready-with-Warnings \u2192 0, Missing Critical Information 6 \u2192 31."}, {"id": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_requirement_ruleset_version", "label": "REQUIREMENT_RULESET_VERSION bump (requirement-rules-2026-09-27-fail-closed-panel-compat)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".local-evidence/golden-r11/R11-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT-PHASES-0-2.md", "source_location": "app/domain/technical-requirement-engine.mjs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ruleset version is part of the profile input fingerprint, so bumping it forces every profile to recompute and apply the new rule; repeated regeneration is then idempotent and creates no version churn."}, {"id": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_standard_subject_in_own_text_gate", "label": "Gate 10 `standard_subject_in_own_text`", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".local-evidence/golden-r11/R11-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT-PHASES-0-2.md", "source_location": "worker/spec-source-fact-promotion.mjs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`resolveGovernedFamily` resolves the subject from the requirement's own text (OWN_TEXT) or the nearest preceding clause (NEAREST_CONTEXT), and every `requirement_standards` row was attributed to that family. Inheritance is sound for an ATTRIBUTE but unsound for a STANDARD. Gate 10 is a pure narrowing gate: a standard is promotable only when the requirement's own text names the family. Verified against live data \u2014 6 of 10 facts now correctly refused."}, {"id": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_compatibility_constraint_vs_target", "label": "Compatibility Constraint vs Target Architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".local-evidence/golden-r11/R11-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT-PHASES-0-2.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Project evidence establishes a CONSTRAINT (single manufacturer, UL listed, SLC Class A, ring topology, approved-vendor list), not a target. The engine already models this correctly and deliberately, and real project-specific compatibility evidence (7 rows) exists but reaches no profile because the owning requirements are not Approved. The compatibility gap is therefore requirement-approval debt, not a model, schema or extraction defect; no `compatibility_constraint` layer is justified and the earlier hypothesis was withdrawn."}, {"id": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_requirement_approval_debt", "label": "Requirement-Approval Debt as Compatibility Blocker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".local-evidence/golden-r11/R11-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT-PHASES-0-2.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_compatibility_relation_extraction", "label": "COMPATIBILITY_RELATION deterministic regex extraction", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".local-evidence/golden-r11/R11-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT-PHASES-0-2.md", "source_location": "app/domain/specification-extractor.mjs:316", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Extraction requires a real 'compatible with / interface with / integrate with' phrase in the sentence. The clause 'c) Compatibility with FlashScan and CLIP protocols.' contains one verbatim, so the FlashScan/CLIP rows are genuine named detection protocols and the extraction is correct \u2014 a hypothesis of inherited-subject mis-scoping was tested and withdrawn."}, {"id": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_service_commercial_path", "label": "Service / Non-Product Commercial Path (confirmed gap)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".local-evidence/golden-r11/R11-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT-PHASES-0-2.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_phase1_panel_compat_fail_closed_repair", "target": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_final_gate_verification_report_panel_compatibility_gate_fail_open", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": ".local-evidence/golden-r11/R11-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT-PHASES-0-2.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_phase1_panel_compat_fail_closed_repair", "target": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_requirement_ruleset_version", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".local-evidence/golden-r11/R11-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT-PHASES-0-2.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_implementation_report_phases_0_2_phase1_panel_compat_fail_closed_repair", "target": "_local_evidence_golden_r11_r11_final_gate_verification_report_fire_alarm_requires_panel_compatibility", "relation": "implements", "confiden